            <ArticleTitle>Acute primary meningoencephalitis from entamoeba Naegleria Fowleri. Report of a clinical case with a favourable outcome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>333-40</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The Authors describe a primary amoebic acute meningoencephalitis case from Naegleria Fowleri, where the parasite was found in the cerebrospinal fluid and in culture. The case had a favorable outcome after treatment with amphotericin B.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
